@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+---
+id: dl-003-clone-json-patch-documents-structurally
+type: decision-log
+title: "Clone JSON Patch documents structurally"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+RFC 6902 operations change a document in sequence, while the public API must
+not mutate its input and only accepts JSON documents.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate JSON values at the public boundary and structurally clone the input
+before applying operations. Clone values inserted by `add`, `replace`, and
+`copy` as well. Use RFC 6901 token parsing and own-property traversal for patch
+paths.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The returned document never shares mutable JSON containers with the input or
+patch values. Invalid JavaScript-only values fail clearly instead of producing
+non-JSON output, and patching keys such as `__proto__` does not alter object
+prototypes.
